/* ==================== Script 323 id="amiyo-gs04-spillcolor" ==================== */
/* GREEN SCREEN Step 4 of 10: ADVANCED SPILL SUPPRESSION + COLOUR CORRECTION (like Ultra Key "Spill Suppression" and "Color Correction").
   Chroma Key (Inspector), new "Spill and colour" section. SPILL: Amount (how much green/blue tint is taken out of the person), Range (low = only clearly green
   pixels, high = also slightly green skin, hair and clothes), Compensation (gives back the brightness the clean-up took away, so skin does not look grey or dark) and
   Desaturate spill (turns leftover tinted spots neutral). The tint removed is the one of your key colour (green or blue, red works too). "Auto spill" sets a good start.
   COLOUR: Saturation, Hue and Luminance of the person after keying, to match them to the new background. Everything starts at 0 = no change, so old projects look the same;
   the tick box "Spill suppression" above still works as before. Not applied while Output view is Alpha / Status. Shows in exports. */
