/* ==================== Script 324 id="amiyo-gs05-mattecleanup" ==================== */
/* GREEN SCREEN Step 5 of 10: MATTE CLEANUP (like Ultra Key "Matte Cleanup": Choke, Soften, Contrast, Mid Point).
   Chroma Key (Inspector), new "Matte cleanup" section, applied in this order to the cut-out edge: CHOKE (+ shrinks the person's outline to eat a green fringe, - grows it back,
   up to 10 pixels, round corners), SOFTEN (blurs the outline 0-10 so it blends in), then CONTRAST and MID POINT (Contrast makes the soft edge crisper again, Mid point decides
   how much of the soft edge counts as "kept": lower keeps more, higher keeps less). Neutral = Choke 0, Soften 0, Contrast 0, Mid point 50, so old projects look the same.
   When the outline grows, the new edge pixels borrow the colour of the person next to them, so no dark halo appears. Works in Alpha / Status view and in exports.
   (The older "Edge shrink" and "Edge blur" sliders above still work and run before this.) */
