/* ==================== Script 326 id="amiyo-gs2-step08-edgecolour" ==================== */
/* GREEN SCREEN plan 2, Step 8 of 10: EDGE COLOUR FIX (not the same as spill).
   Chroma Key (Inspector), new "Edge colour" box under Garbage matte. The soft edge of the person (hair, fingers, the outline) is a MIX of the person and the green behind. Spill clean-up
   only removes green TINT; this fixes the colour itself, in two ways:
   EDGE COLOUR FIX: for every half-see-through edge pixel it works out what the person's colour would be without the green mixed in (it estimates the green right next to it, so uneven screens
   work too) and puts that colour back. BORROW FROM INSIDE: edge pixels, and the solid pixels just inside the outline, take on the colour of the person a little further in, which removes a stubborn
   green or dark fringe. EDGE WIDTH: how far (in pixels) the edge area reaches. It runs before the new background, light wrap and shadow are added, so the new background never gets the green.
   Everything is 0 = off by default, so old projects look the same. Not applied in Alpha / Status view. Shows in the preview and the export. */
