      '<div class="note">Pick where the AI runs. Ollama, local servers (LM Studio, llama.cpp, Jan) and Chrome AI stay on your device. The free online services (Pollinations, LLM7, Airforce, DeepInfra, Hack Club AI, mlvoca, ch.at, G4F, AI Horde text, Puter) need no key, so your prompt is sent to them. On-device browser AI (WebLLM) keeps everything on this phone but downloads a model once and needs WebGPU. Pick a model from each list, or leave it on Auto and the app picks one and switches to another if it fails.</div>'+
      '<label class="nm" for="aiHubQF">Show</label><select id="aiHubQF" aria-label="Show which models"><option value="">All models</option><option value="fast">Fast ones</option><option value="smart">Smart ones</option><option value="code">Good for code</option><option value="sees pictures">Can see pictures</option></select><label class="nm" for="aiHubQuick">Quick pick a model</label><select id="aiHubQuick" aria-label="Quick pick a model"></select><div class="note">Your pick is tried first. If it fails, the app switches to the next model on its own.</div><label class="nm" for="aiHubMode">Use</label><select id="aiHubMode"></select><div id="aiHubCards"></div>'+
      '<div class="row"><button type="button" class="go" id="aiHubCheckAll" style="flex:1">Check every model (and sort by speed)</button></div><div class="row"><button type="button" class="go" id="aiHubTestAll" style="flex:1">Test all</button><button type="button" id="aiHubReset" style="flex:1">Retry paused</button></div>'+
      '<details id="aiHubStats"><summary style="min-height:44px;display:flex;align-items:center;color:#ffb454">Speed and reliability</summary><div id="aiHubStatsBody" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px"></div><div class="row" style="margin-top:8px"><button type="button" class="go" id="aiHubBench" style="flex:1">Speed test</button><button type="button" id="aiHubSort" style="flex:1">Sort by speed</button></div><div class="row" style="margin-top:8px"><button type="button" id="aiHubStatsClear" style="flex:1">Clear stats</button></div><div class="note">Sort keeps on-device providers (Ollama, local, Chrome) ahead of online ones, so your text is never moved to a website just because it is faster.</div><div class="st" id="aiHubStatsOut" role="status"></div></details>'+
      '<div class="row"><button type="button" id="aiHubExp" style="flex:1">Export settings</button><button type="button" id="aiHubImp" style="flex:1">Import settings</button><input type="file" id="aiHubFile" accept=".json,application/json" style="display:none"></div><div class="st" id="aiHubOut" role="status"></div></div>';
